<title>GERMANY: Opel extends Herman contract for five years.</title>
<headline>Opel extends Herman contract for five years.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Adam Opel AG, a unit of General Motors Corp, said on Friday it has extended the contract of Opel Managing Director David Herman for five more years.</p>
<p>Opel said in a statement that the supervisory board cited Herman's efforts to improve the competitiveness of Opel's plants in Germany as one reason for extending his contract.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
